meta {
  name: Probe modem-native IMS once (read-only)
  type: http
  seq: 181
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/modem/lines/{{line_id}}/native/ims/probe
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

body:json {
  {}
}

docs {
  Explicit user-triggered read-only probe, not a passive GET. Requires an already-owned native QMI controller with explicit AT endpoint,
  qualified EC20-CE-FAG revision and positively matched slot/ICCID before and after the query.
  Both host IMS enable intents and all host LTE/WLAN session/flow/cleanup ownership must be absent. The endpoint never disables them for you.
  No URC/NV/profile/bearer changes; the exact one-argument QIMSCFG ims_status form is used once. No automatic retry or takeover.
  Cancellation keeps the physical and host-exclusion guards until the bounded driver transaction finishes; repeated probes return busy.
  401 unauthorized, 404 line missing, 409 busy/binding changed, 501 adapter/firmware unsupported, 503 observation unavailable, 502 malformed reply.
  Only {} is accepted; callers cannot supply AT commands, SIM identities or enable flags. Modem observations never change host readiness or fees.
}
